INT. DEEP-SPACE HABITAT - COMMON ROOM - NIGHT CYCLE

Dim amber lighting. A long table bolted to the floor, six mugs, a hydroponic wall of drooping lettuce. A viewport shows a black field of stars. Outside, nothing.

MAYA THORNQUIST (40s, station chief, ponytail) pours coffee substitute. DR. AMBROSE BEAUMONT (60s, botanist, cardigan) pokes at a lettuce leaf. TARIQ SALEH (30s, engineer, wrench in his belt) stares at his tablet. LINNEA SORENSEN (20s, comms officer) eats a protein bar. KOFI MENSAH (30s, medic, stethoscope) sketches in a notebook. And GRIGORI PETROV (50s, security, arms folded) leans on the wall.

MAYA
Morning, everyone.

LINNEA
It's night cycle.

MAYA
Morning for me.

Light chuckles. Tariq doesn't look up from his tablet. Kofi turns a page. Grigori's jaw works.

TARIQ
Maya, the coolant readings are off again.

MAYA
How off?

TARIQ
Point three. Same as yesterday.

MAYA
Same as yesterday is fine.

TARIQ
Same as yesterday is a trend.

MAYA
(to the room)
Tariq thinks we're going to explode.

AMBROSE
We might.

LINNEA
Ambrose, don't.

AMBROSE
It's a statistical possibility.

KOFI
Everything is.

Grigori pushes off the wall and crosses to the table. He sits. He doesn't speak.

MAYA
Grigori, you're quiet.

GRIGORI
Am I?

MAYA
You're always quiet.

GRIGORI
Then I'm normal.

Linnea snorts. Ambrose smiles, pleased. Tariq finally sets down his tablet.

TARIQ
Maya. I need to say something.

MAYA
Go ahead.

TARIQ
I think someone's been tampering with the cooling loop.

The room stills. Kofi's pencil stops. Ambrose lowers his leaf.

MAYA
Someone.

TARIQ
Someone on board.

GRIGORI
That's a serious accusation.

TARIQ
It's a serious loop.

MAYA
(to the room)
Does anyone know anything about this?

Nobody answers. The lights pulse, dim, brighten. Linnea's bar crumbles in her fist. Grigori's chair creaks.

MAYA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Of course.

KOFI
Maya?

MAYA
Nothing.

A low tone rings through the hull. Not an alarm. Deeper. The amber lights flicker to red.

LINNEA
That's the pressure alert.

TARIQ
That's not the pressure alert. That's the coolant.

AMBROSE
Is it the end?

MAYA
It's not the end.

GRIGORI
(softly)
It might be.

Everyone turns to look at him. His hand has found something in his pocket.
